{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Withdrawn",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed single-storey rear extension, by virtue of its scale, siting and combined depth together with the existing projection(s), would provide for an excessively large extension, which lacks any sense of subservience to the host dwelling. With a footprint at ca. 50% of the original rear garden space, this adds to a sense of overdevelopment, which is considered harmful to the character and appearance of no. 85 Kings Road. As such the proposal fails to comply with the design objectives of Policy 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed extension, by virtue of its scale and siting in relation to no. 85 Kings Road, would create an oppressive, overbearing sense of enclosure, which is to the detriment of continued enjoyment of the private amenity space. This is considered harmful to residential amenity and is therefore contrary to the objectives of Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
